From aa859b10eed7308d84456fe374e54721dbfecbd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bcup02 <55205420+bcup02@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:22:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: exchange-agnostic verified-close-backfill core
 (v0.14.0) (#10)

New verified_close_backfill module: builds a schema-1.0 evidence dict from a
local trade_open + normalized exchange fills (the same reconcile-source/v1
shape binance_reconcile_fetch.fill_rows already emits), then appends the
evidence-backed repair events (reconciliation_evidence_recorded / fill /
trade_close / position_reconciled_closed) via an injected ledger_append
callable -- never constructs an exchange client or a project's own
TradeLedger, so any exchange adapter emitting the normalized fill shape can
feed it and any project's own ledger class can consume it.

Ported (not copied) from momentum's fetch_verified_close_evidence.py /
append_reconciled_close.py, which hardcode Binance's raw field names deep in
the evidence builder and a "method": "read_only_mexc_history_orders_and_deals"
string that's been wrong since momentum's Binance migration. Fixed here:
method is now a parameter threaded through from whichever adapter actually
fetched the evidence, defaulting to a neutral label for old evidence that
predates the field entirely (proven against momentum's real MUBARAK evidence
fixture, which has neither a "method" field nor Binance-shaped fields at
all -- MEXC-era numeric exchange_side codes pass through untouched).

binance_reconcile_fetch.position_rows / .fill_rows made public (renamed from
_position_rows / _fill_rows, pure rename, no logic change) so a project's
verified-close CLI can call them directly for a narrow symbol+window query
without going through the heavier full fetch() (balance, open orders, ...).

Momentum's own two tools will be refactored to consume this in a follow-up
PR; this PR only adds the shared core and does not change any consuming
project yet.

Co-authored-by: bcup02 <columnbb@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
